This is an excellent business requirement. You are transitioning the Status Screen from a simple "My Requests" page into a **Global Dashboard for Approvers**, while keeping it restricted for standard Makers.
The beautiful thing about the frontend code you just shared is that **it is already perfectly designed to handle this!** Because we previously wrote the isViewingSelfCreated check, if an Approver opens a batch they didn't create, the "Cancel Voucher Batch" button will automatically hide itself to protect the data!
To make this work, the heavy lifting actually needs to happen in your **Spring Boot Backend SQL**. The frontend just needs to pass the roleId to the backend so the database knows who is looking.
Here are the **2 steps** to implement this logic perfectly.
### Step 1: The Frontend Update (VoucherPostingStatus.jsx)
We need to grab the user's roleId from the browser's storage (just like we did for the Maker screen) and pass it into the API call.
**Find your fetchMyBatches function (around line 351) and replace the API call block with this:**
```javascript
